IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `written-law-interface`
IMPORT `mda-types`

-- Misuse of Drugs Act 1973: the powers of the Central Narcotics Bureau and the other officers (ss 24 to 26, 30 to 32), forfeiture (ss 27, 28), and the court
-- (s 53).
-- Source: source/MDA1973.txt lines 1701 to 1860 (ss 24 to 26), 2004 to 2087 (ss 27, 28), 2089 to 2427 (ss 30 to 32), 3786 to 3796 (s 53).
--
-- The question this module answers: WHO MAY DO WHAT, AND WHERE IS THE CASE HEARD?  Part 3 gives officers of the Bureau, police officers, special police
-- officers and (some) officers of customs powers to enter, search, arrest, require specimens and seize; s 32 gives the Bureau's officers the powers of a
-- police officer under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for an investigation of an arrestable offence; s 53 gives the District Court and the Magistrate's Court
-- jurisdiction.  The answers the Code needs (an arrestable offence; the District Court) are in `the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973's statement about its offences`,
-- a record declared in written-law-interface.l4.
--
-- Not encoded: the conduct of the search (24(2) break open any door, window, lock and so on; 25(2) and (4) take the arrested person and the thing to the
-- Bureau, a police station or a customs station; 26(2A) directions to the operator of an autonomous vehicle or unmanned aircraft), the sale and disposal
-- of a seized item (26A) and of a forfeited thing (29), the Bureau's arms (32A), and the treatment, rehabilitation and inquiry Parts 4 to 6.

§ `The officers`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'police officer', 'special police officer', 'officer of customs', 'senior officer of customs'; ss 24(1), 25(1), 26(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is a police officer of any rank` IF
        r EQUALS `a police officer not below the rank of sergeant`
    OR  r EQUALS `a police officer below the rank of sergeant`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 2 'officer of customs', 'senior officer of customs'"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is an officer of customs` IF
        r EQUALS `a senior officer of customs`
    OR  r EQUALS `an officer of customs who is not a senior officer of customs`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'officer of the Bureau'"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` IF
        r EQUALS `an officer of the Bureau`
    OR  r EQUALS `the Director of the Central Narcotics Bureau`

§ `24. Powers of search and seizure`

-- 24(1): any officer of the Bureau, police officer, special police officer or SENIOR officer of customs (an officer of customs who is not senior is not
-- named) may at any time (a) without a warrant enter and search any place or premises in which he reasonably suspects there is to be found (i) a controlled drug,
-- controlled substance, psychoactive substance or article liable to seizure, (ia) a vehicle, autonomous vehicle, unmanned aircraft, unmanned vessel or component
-- used in or in connection with an offence under the Act, or (ii) a person who has committed or is reasonably suspected to have committed an offence under
-- the Act or an arrestable offence under the regulations; (b) search any person found there; and (c) seize and detain what he reasonably suspects is a
-- controlled drug, controlled substance, psychoactive substance, an article liable to seizure, or such a vehicle.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 24(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is one section 24(1) names` IF
        `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` r
    OR  `the officer is a police officer of any rank` r
    OR  r EQUALS `a special police officer`
    OR  r EQUALS `a senior officer of customs`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 24(1)(a)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Premises Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may without a warrant enter and search the place or premises` IF
        `the officer is one section 24(1) names` r
    AND (   s's `the officer reasonably suspects that there is to be found in the place or premises a controlled drug, controlled substance, psychoactive substance or article liable to seizure`
         OR s's `the officer reasonably suspects that there is to be found in the place or premises a vehicle, autonomous vehicle, unmanned aircraft, unmanned vessel or component used in the commission of or in connection with an offence under this Act`
         OR s's `the officer reasonably suspects that there is to be found in the place or premises a person who has committed or is reasonably suspected to have committed an offence under this Act or an arrestable offence under the regulations`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 24(1)(b)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Premises Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may search a person found in the place or premises` IF
    `the officer may without a warrant enter and search the place or premises` r s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 24(1)(c)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Premises Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may seize and detain what is found` IF
        `the officer may without a warrant enter and search the place or premises` r s
    AND s's `the officer reasonably suspects that a thing found is a controlled drug, controlled substance or psychoactive substance, or an article liable to seizure`

§ `25 and 25A. Powers of arrest; bail and bond`

-- 25(1): any officer of the Bureau, police officer, special police officer or officer of customs (here ANY officer of customs) may arrest and search without a
-- warrant any person who has committed or whom he reasonably suspects to have committed an offence under the Act or an arrestable offence under the
-- regulations.  25(3): "A woman must not be searched under this Act except by another woman."  25(2), (4): the arrested person and things are taken to the
-- Bureau, a police station or a customs station and may be searched; the officer may seize and detain.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 25(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is one section 25(1) names` IF
        `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` r
    OR  `the officer is a police officer of any rank` r
    OR  r EQUALS `a special police officer`
    OR  `the officer is an officer of customs` r

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 25(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, a IS AN `Arrest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may arrest and search the person without a warrant` IF
        `the officer is one section 25(1) names` r
    AND (   a's `the person has committed an offence under this Act or an arrestable offence under the regulations`
         OR a's `the officer reasonably suspects that the person has committed an offence under this Act or an arrestable offence under the regulations`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 25(3)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, a IS AN `Arrest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the search of the person arrested is permitted` IF
        `the officer may arrest and search the person without a warrant` r a
    AND (   NOT a's `the person to be searched is a woman`
         OR a's `the searcher is a woman`)

-- 25A(1): a person arrested by an officer of the Bureau, police officer, special police officer or officer of customs under 25(1) may be released on bail or on
-- personal bond granted by any officer of the Bureau.  25A(2): Division 5 (Bails and bonds) of Part 6 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 applies with the
-- references to "officer", "police officer" and "police officer of or above the rank of sergeant" read to include an officer of the Bureau, and the
-- reference to the Commissioner of Police in section 92(1) read to include the Director.  (The Code's bail rules are not encoded here.)
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 25A(1)"
GIVEN `the person was arrested under section 25(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, grantor IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be released on bail or on personal bond granted by the grantor` IF
        `the person was arrested under section 25(1)`
    AND `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` grantor

§ `26. Power to search ship, hovercraft, etc., and person arriving in or departing from Singapore`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 26(1)(a), (b)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Vessel Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may stop, board and search the ship, hovercraft, aircraft, vehicle or train and search the persons in it` IF
        `the officer is one section 25(1) names` r
    AND s's `the officer has reason to suspect that there is in the ship, hovercraft, aircraft, vehicle or train a controlled drug in contravention of this Act, a controlled substance, a psychoactive substance or an article liable to seizure`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 26(1)(ba)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Vessel Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may intercept and search the autonomous vehicle, unmanned aircraft or unmanned vessel` IF
        `the officer is one section 25(1) names` r
    AND s's `the officer has reason to suspect that there is in the autonomous vehicle, unmanned aircraft or unmanned vessel a controlled drug or controlled substance, a psychoactive substance or an article liable to seizure`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 26(1)(c)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Vessel Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may search the person arriving in or about to depart from Singapore` IF
        `the officer is one section 25(1) names` r
    AND s's `the person is arriving in Singapore or about to depart from Singapore`

§ `27 and 28. Forfeiture`

-- 27(3): "An order for the forfeiture of any controlled drug, controlled substance, psychoactive substance or article is to be made if it is proved to the
-- satisfaction of a court that an offence under this Act has been committed and that such drug, substance or article was the subject matter of or was used in the
-- commission of the offence even though no person may have been convicted of that offence."  27(4): if there is no prosecution, the thing is deemed forfeited
-- to the Government on the expiry of one month from the seizure unless a claim has been made before then in the prescribed manner.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 27(3)"
GIVEN f IS A `Forfeiture Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order for the forfeiture of the drug, substance or article is to be made` IF
        f's `it is proved to the satisfaction of a court that an offence under this Act has been committed`
    AND f's `the drug, substance or article was the subject matter of or was used in the commission of the offence`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 27(4)"
GIVEN f IS A `Forfeiture Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the drug, substance or article is deemed to be forfeited to the Government` IF
        f's `there is no prosecution with regard to the drug, substance or article seized`
    AND f's `one month has expired from the date of the seizure`
    AND NOT f's `a claim to it was made before that date in the prescribed manner`

-- 28(1): where a person has been convicted of an offence under the Act, the court MAY order forfeited any ship, hovercraft, aircraft, unmanned aircraft,
-- unmanned vessel or component proved to have been used in connection with the offence.  28(2): the court IS TO, on the Public Prosecutor's application, order
-- forfeited any vehicle, autonomous vehicle or component so proved.  28(3): the section does not apply to a ship, hovercraft or unmanned vessel of more than 200
-- tons net or an aircraft or unmanned aircraft belonging to a person carrying on a regular passenger service to and from Singapore by means of it.  28(4): none is
-- to be forfeited if its owner establishes that it was unlawfully in the possession of another person without the owner's consent.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 28(1), (3) and (4)"
GIVEN f IS A `Forfeiture Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order forfeiture of the ship, hovercraft, aircraft or unmanned craft` IF
        f's `a person has been convicted of an offence under this Act`
    AND f's `the ship, hovercraft, aircraft, unmanned aircraft or unmanned vessel, or a component, has been proved to have been used in any manner in connection with the offence`
    AND NOT f's `the ship, hovercraft or unmanned vessel is of more than 200 tons net, or the aircraft or unmanned aircraft belongs to a person carrying on a regular passenger service to and from Singapore by means of it`
    AND NOT f's `the owner establishes that it was unlawfully in the possession of another person without the owner's consent`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 28(2) and (4)"
GIVEN f IS A `Forfeiture Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is to order forfeiture of the vehicle` IF
        f's `a person has been convicted of an offence under this Act`
    AND f's `the vehicle, autonomous vehicle or a component has been proved to have been used in any manner in connection with the offence`
    AND f's `the Public Prosecutor applies for the order`
    AND NOT f's `the owner establishes that it was unlawfully in the possession of another person without the owner's consent`

§ `30. Obstruction of inspection or search`

-- 30(1): an offence to (a) obstruct any officer of the Bureau, police officer, officer of customs or other public officer in the exercise of a power under the Act;
-- (b) fail to comply with a lawful requirement of such an officer in the execution of his duty under the Act; (c) without reasonable excuse fail to furnish
-- information in his possession required by such an officer; or (d) furnish to such an officer information which he knows or has reason to believe to be false.
-- 30(2): "public officer" includes a special police officer exercising a power under section 24, 25 or 26.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 30(1)(a)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Obstruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 30(1)(a) is made out` IF
    o's `the accused obstructed an officer of the Bureau, police officer, officer of customs or other public officer in the exercise of a power under this Act`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 30(1)(b)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Obstruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 30(1)(b) is made out` IF
    o's `the accused failed to comply with a lawful requirement of such an officer in the execution of his or her duty under this Act`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 30(1)(c)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Obstruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 30(1)(c) is made out` IF
    o's `the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed to furnish information in his or her possession required by such an officer`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 30(1)(d)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Obstruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 30(1)(d) is made out` IF
    o's `the accused furnished to such an officer information which he or she knew or had reason to believe to be false`

§ `31, 31A, 31B. Urine, hair and oral fluid tests`

-- 31(1): any officer of the Bureau, immigration officer or police officer not below the rank of SERGEANT may, if he reasonably suspects a person to have committed an
-- offence under 8(b) or 11I(1)(b), require that person to provide a specimen of urine.  31(1B): a serving member of the Singapore Armed Forces appointed by the
-- Minister as an enforcement officer may do so for a person subject to military law.  31(1A): the Director may, to ensure that a relevant person is no longer a drug
-- addict, after the relevant time, order the relevant person to present himself and to provide a specimen.  31A(1), (1A) are the same for hair (without 31(1B));
-- 31B(1) is the same for oral fluid (no 31(1B), no Director's order).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 31(1), 31A(1), 31B(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is one section 31(1) names` IF
        `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` r
    OR  r EQUALS `an immigration officer`
    OR  r EQUALS `a police officer not below the rank of sergeant`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31(1) and (1B)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may require a specimen of urine` IF
        s's `the officer reasonably suspects that the person has committed an offence under section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b)`
    AND (   `the officer is one section 31(1) names` r
         OR r EQUALS `a serving member of the Singapore Armed Forces appointed by the Minister as an enforcement officer`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 31A(1), 31B(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may require a specimen of hair or oral fluid` IF
        s's `the officer reasonably suspects that the person has committed an offence under section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b)`
    AND `the officer is one section 31(1) names` r

-- 31(2): a person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to provide a specimen of urine within the time required by an officer referred to in 31(1), (1A) or (1B)
-- commits an offence (punished by section 33(3A), the Schedule's row 31(2) being deleted); 31(2A): without reasonable excuse fails to comply with the Director's
-- order (Second Schedule 31(2A)); 31A(2), (2A) for hair; 31B(2) for oral fluid.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31(2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 31(2) is made out` IF
        `the officer may require a specimen of urine` r s
    AND s's `the person failed, without reasonable excuse, to provide the specimen within the time required`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31(2A) and (1A)"
GIVEN s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 31(2A) is made out` IF
        s's `the Director has ordered a relevant person to present himself or herself and to provide a specimen, to ensure the person is no longer a drug addict`
    AND s's `the person failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the Director's order`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31A(2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 31A(2) is made out` IF
        `the officer may require a specimen of hair or oral fluid` r s
    AND s's `the person failed, without reasonable excuse, to provide the specimen within the time required`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31B(2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 31B(2) is made out` IF
        `the officer may require a specimen of hair or oral fluid` r s
    AND s's `the person failed, without reasonable excuse, to provide the specimen within the time required`

-- 31(4): a urine specimen "must be divided into 3 parts" and (a) a preliminary urine test conducted on one part; (b) each of the remaining 2 parts marked and
-- sealed and a urine test conducted on each part by a DIFFERENT person, being an analyst of the Health Sciences Authority or a person the Minister appoints.
-- 31(5): where the preliminary test is negative, the officer may either discard the remaining 2 parts or proceed under 31(4)(b).  The consumption presumption of
-- section 22 needs BOTH tests of 31(4)(b) (mda-presumptions.l4).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31(4) and (5)"
GIVEN s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the urine specimen has been dealt with as section 31(4) requires` IF
        s's `the specimen of urine was divided into 3 parts and a preliminary urine test was conducted on one part`
    AND s's `each of the remaining 2 parts was marked and sealed and a urine test was conducted on each part by a different person, being an analyst of the Health Sciences Authority or a person appointed by the Minister`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 31(5)"
GIVEN s IS A `Specimen Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may discard the remaining 2 parts of the specimen` IF
    s's `the preliminary urine test was negative for controlled drugs and psychoactive substances`

§ `32. Power of investigation of officers of the Bureau`

-- 32(1): in any case relating to the commission of an offence under the Act, an officer of the Bureau has all the powers of a police officer under the Criminal
-- Procedure Code 2010 in relation to an investigation into an ARRESTABLE offence.  32(2): for an offence under the regulations, the powers for an arrestable
-- offence if it is arrestable, and for a non-arrestable offence if it is not.  32(3): for (1) and (2)(a), an officer of the Bureau exercising them "is deemed to be an
-- officer not below the rank of inspector of police".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 32(1), (2) and (3)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, `the case relates to the commission of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer has all the powers of a police officer in relation to an investigation into an arrestable offence` IF
        `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` r
    AND `the case relates to the commission of an offence under this Act`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 32(3)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed to be an officer not below the rank of inspector of police` IF
    `the officer is an officer of the Bureau` r

§ `53. Jurisdiction of courts`

-- 53: "A District Court or a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine all proceedings under this Act and, despite anything to the contrary in the
-- Criminal Procedure Code 2010, a District Court has power to impose the full penalty or punishment in respect of any offence provided by this Act EXCEPT THE
-- PUNISHMENT OF DEATH."  The statement the Code reads (written-law-interface.l4) says FALSE for a Magistrate's Court: the encoding reads "all proceedings" as
-- proceedings within a Magistrate's Court's sentencing powers, which the Code decides, and leaves the trial of an offence beyond them to ss 7 to 9 of the Code
-- (fork F7 in NOTES.md).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 53"
GIVEN c IS A `Court Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court has power to impose the punishment` IF
    NOT c's `the punishment in question is the punishment of death`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 25(1), 53"
GIVETH A `Written Law Procedure Statement`
`the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973's statement about its offences` MEANS
    `Written Law Procedure Statement` WITH
        `the Act` IS "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973"
        `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE
        `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS TRUE
        `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS TRUE
        `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS FALSE
